"body": "Hello fellow farmers! I wanted to share a practical tip that has been extremely useful during our calving season nights. As a 33-year-old software tester, I don't have the luxury of being on the farm during the day, but I still want to do my part in helping out during the busy calving season. Here it is: Invest in a good quality, red or amber night light for your barn. This simple addition can significantly reduce stress levels for both mother and calf during birth, as well as improve your own visibility without startling the animals. It has made all the difference for us this year! I hope this tip helps someone out there who may be in a similar situation. Happy calving season!"
